--- Finding (json_pointer): a value that is only ever an error — `error['why']`
--- itself, or a variable that holds nothing else — handed to `encode` or `str`
--- does not build compiled. (A function's answer that can fail or succeed
--- builds: `encode[f[-1]]` is fine.)
---
--- Interpreted (crow run -i):
---     error: line 22: why
---     error: line 23: why
--- Compiled (crow run):
---     error[E0277]: the trait bound `!: ToJson` is not satisfied
---       --> src/main.rs:36
---     error: the compiled program does not build — the Rust compiler refused
---     what Crow accepted, a bug in Crow, not in this program
---   (with the encode line taken out, str's line: error[E0308]: mismatched types)
--- The generated call hands the builtin the payload of a value that has none:
---   … else { CrowResult { ok: true, value: crow_runtime::json::encode(&(unreachable!())), … } }
--- `unreachable!()` is `!`, which implements no ToJson.
--- Expected: the interpreter's output in both modes — by Auto-Propagation
--- (spec section 10) a builtin handed an error value answers that error
--- without running; the encode row's "an error value as null" is an error
--- inside a list or a record.
log[encode[error['why']]]
log[str[error['why']]]
